            "old_string": "### 52.1 StarterUnion bitmask gating for DAAC post-filter\n- [ ] DEFERRED (see CHANGELOG.md for benchmark results): initial\n      implementation showed +2.1% overhead, not improvement, because\n      LeftmostLongest AC means every hit is valid.  Revisit only if\n      architecture changes to Standard-mode AC (multi-match).\n  - Inspired by `externals/opencc-fmmseg` StarterUnion: a two-tier\n      (BMP dense array + astral sparse map) per-starter bitmask that\n      prunes impossible (starter, length) pairs after DAAC match but\n      before predicate IR evaluation.\n  - For each starter character, precompute a `u64` bitmask where bit N\n    means a pattern of char-length N+1 exists starting with that\n    character, plus a `u8` max-length cap.  BMP starters\n    (U+0000..U+FFFF) use dense `[u64; 65536]` + `[u8; 65536]` arrays\n    (~576 KB).  Astral starters use `FxHashMap<char, (u64, u8)>`.\n  - Bit indexing: bit N represents char-length N+1 (not byte-length).\n    Use `checked_shl(len - 1)` to avoid overflow for lengths >= 64.\n    For patterns with char-length > 64, fall through to unconditional\n    predicate evaluation (max_len cap still prunes).\n  - Build the union once in `Scanner::new()` from\n    `CompiledSpellingDb` patterns (wrap in `Arc` for thread safety).\n    In the AC match callback (`spelling.rs`), before evaluating\n    predicates for a match at position P with char-length L: check\n    `union.mask(input[P]) & checked_shl(1u64, L - 1)` -- if zero,\n    skip predicate evaluation entirely.\n  - Also: use descending-bit iteration (`leading_zeros()` loop) from\n    opencc-fmmseg `for_each_len_dec` for longest-match-first probe\n    order in overlap resolution.\n  - Prerequisite: benchmark first to confirm predicate dispatch is\n    still a measurable cost post-50.x.  If <3% of spelling time,\n    defer.\n  - Scope: new `src/engine/scan/starter_union.rs`, changes to\n    `src/engine/scan/spelling.rs` (match callback), `mod.rs`\n    (Scanner::new union build).\n  - Gate: `cargo bench --bench scanner` shows measurable improvement\n    on `spelling_only` and `full_default`.  Identical scan output.\n    Memory: +576 KB for BMP arrays (acceptable given spelling = 86%\n    of CPU).",
