            "content": "# CLAUDE.md\n\nRust MCP server for zh-TW text linting against MoE standards. Enforces vocabulary, punctuation, and orthographic conventions specific to Taiwan. `zhtw` tool with `max_errors` acts as an output gate.\n\n## Build & Test\n\n```bash\ncargo build                   # debug\ncargo build --release         # release\ncargo test                    # all tests\ncargo clippy                  # must be warning-free\ncargo fmt --check             # format check\n```\n\nRequires Rust 1.91+ (see `rust-toolchain.toml`).\n\n## Key Commands\n\n```bash\ncargo run                                        # MCP server (stdio)\ncargo run -- lint <file>                         # lint file\ncargo run -- lint file.md --fix                  # auto-fix in-place\ncargo run -- lint file.md --format sarif         # SARIF output\ncargo run -- lint file.md --explain              # show context per issue\ncargo run -- lint file.md --detect-ai            # AI writing detection\ncargo run -- lint docs/ --diff-from main         # lint changed files only\ncargo run -- convert file.md                     # SC->TC conversion\ncargo run -- tm list|record|export|import|clear  # translation memory\n```\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nsrc/\n  main.rs          CLI + colored output + --fix/--explain/SARIF\n  engine/\n    scan/\n      mod.rs       Scanner, ContentType, ScratchSpace, bench helpers\n      spelling.rs  Spelling AC (charwise daachorse + bytewise fallback)\n      rule_ir.rs   Compiled predicate IR, CompiledSpellingDb, ProfileFilter\n      punctuation.rs, spacing.rs, ellipsis.rs, quotes.rs, overlap.rs, grammar.rs\n    segment.rs     MMSEG segmenter + CharTrie + BoundaryBitmap\n    ai_score.rs    Document-level AI signature scoring\n    excluded.rs    Exclusion zones (URLs, paths, code fences)\n    lineindex.rs   Line/column mapping (UTF-16 columns for LSP)\n    normalize.rs   NFC normalization with byte-offset mapping\n    s2t.rs         SC->TC converter\n  mcp/\n    tools.rs       MCP tool handler (zhtw: unified lint/fix/gate)\n    sampling.rs    LLM disambiguation via sampling/createMessage\n    transport.rs   Synchronous stdio JSON-RPC transport\n  rules/\n    ruleset.rs     SpellingRule, Issue, Profile, ProfileConfig\n    store.rs       Override/Suppression/Pack/TM stores\n    loader.rs      Embedded ruleset loader\nassets/\n  ruleset.json     1106 spelling + 15 case rules\n```\n\n## Ruleset Conventions\n\n- Vocabulary conforms to MoE dictionary (https://www.moedict.tw/). MoE meaning takes precedence over colloquial or cross-strait borrowed usage.\n- Dual-meaning terms MUST have `context_clues` to restrict firing to the intended domain.\n- `to: []` means no zh translation; `english` field shown as suggestion.\n- `english` field disambiguates cross-strait terms. Slash separates variants; most common first.\n- Variant rules (`type: \"variant\"`) require exactly 1 `to` entry; skipped on Simplified input.\n- `(@seealso X, Y)` cross-references related rules. Context uses \"tw\"/\"cn\" (not country names).\n\n## Development\n\n- **localhost** (macOS): build, test, lint.\n- **node1** (`ssh node1`): Linux x86_64, 64-core. Benchmark target.\n  ```\n  rsync -az --exclude target --exclude '.git' . node1:~/playground/zhtw-mcp/\n  ssh node1 'export RUSTUP_HOME=~/.rustup2 CARGO_HOME=~/.cargo2 PATH=~/.cargo2/bin:$PATH && cd ~/playground/zhtw-mcp && cargo bench --bench scanner'\n  ```\n- No backward compatibility guarantees. Update every call site on API changes.\n\n## Code Style\n\n- `rustfmt` defaults, `clippy` clean, `anyhow` at binary boundaries\n- All public types derive `Serialize`/`Deserialize`\n- No async runtime. Logs to stderr; stdout reserved for JSON-RPC.\n- Unit tests co-located (`#[cfg(test)] mod tests`). New filenames use hyphens.\n- Never `git commit`/`push`/`reset` unless explicitly requested.\n- Never include `TODO.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, or `CLAUDE.md` in git commits or `.gitignore`. These are local-only files.\n",
